/* Generated by tools/make_tables.py from tools/descriptions.py (owner-approved texts; do not edit). {quest index (0..55) whose bit selects
 * AFTER, -1 one text; BEFORE (or the only text); AFTER}. Index = quest item n (F077 + n). */
static const qj_item_text qj_item_texts[85] = {
    /* item-52 */ {-1, "A crisp deed bearing the King's seal. For 50,000 gold Ebenezer the Taxman sold you the land on which an old ruined castle rests. It isn't much to look at yet, but the King's engineers will happily build on it - for a price.", NULL},
    /* item-53 */ {-1, "A key cut from clear crystal, cold to the touch. Valia the Old Woman pressed it into your hands so that you might enter the witches' tower in Toad Meadow and destroy them.", NULL},
    /* item-54 */ {22, "A key carved from a single yellowed bone, found at the very top of the Tower of High Magic. Its teeth are shaped like tiny fingers. Whatever door it opens, its owner did not want visitors.", "A key carved from a single yellowed bone. It opens Baron Darzog's tower - and beyond Darzog's tower, Crodo says, lies the way into the clouds and to Castle Xeen itself."},
    /* item-55 */ {-1, "A key that hums faintly with bound magic, bought for 300 gems deep inside the Cave of Illusion. It opens the Tower of High Magic, where the lore of sorcerers is kept far from curious hands.", NULL},
    /* item-56 */ {-1, "A heavy amulet set with a jewel shaped like a sphinx's eye. Arie the Apprentice gave it to you for recovering the Scroll of Insight. The great Sphinx of the north is said to admit only those who wear it.", NULL},
    /* item-57 */ {-1, "A dark, oily stone found by the workers clearing rubble at your new castle. Staring into it brings on a shiver you cannot explain. Somewhere a dungeon of terrors waits for its key.", NULL},
    /* item-58 */ {-1, "A smooth grey stone found while the keep of your castle was being built. It is warm, and very faintly it seems to pulse, like a slow stone heart. Golems are said to step aside for whoever carries one.", NULL},
    /* item-59 */ {-1, "A rough stone marked with the horned sign of Yak, given to you by Mirabeth the Mermaid. It opens the temple of the evil Clerics of Yak, where the Elixir of Restoration is kept.", NULL},
    /* item-5A */ {23, "Lord Xeen's own scepter, taken from his remains. Time itself seems to bend and stutter around it. Such a thing should not be left lying about, and surely the great powers of this world would want to know of it.", "Lord Xeen's own scepter, taken from his remains; time seems to stutter around it. It is no mirror, but King Burlock asked you to bring him what was found near the great volcano. He may well want to see this."},
    /* item-5B */ {3, "A spiralled unicorn horn that glows softly in your hands, found in the highest room of the witches' tower. There is great healing power in it. Whoever lost such a treasure must be grieving.", "The Alacorn of the unicorn Falista, taken back from the witches of Toad Meadow. Valia the Old Woman is waiting for it; with its magic she hopes to bring Falista back to life."},
    /* item-5C */ {10, "A small flask of shimmering liquid stolen from the Clerics of Yak. One sip is said to undo any curse of change, returning a creature to its true form.", "The Elixir of Restoration, stolen from the Clerics of Yak. Mirabeth the Mermaid waits for it - with it she can win back the beauty and the tail that a jealous sorceress took from her."},
    /* item-5D */ {11, "A slender wand of pale wood, tipped with a tiny star, found where the crazed sprites roam. It tingles in your hand, as if it wishes it were somewhere else.", "The Wand of Faery Magic. Danulf the Faery King wants it back from the sprites who stole it - without it his powers fade, and the sprites, drunk with its power, attack anyone in the forest."},
    /* item-5E */ {7, "A diamond tiara fit for royalty, found among the loot of the robbers of Rivercity. It is far too fine to have been honestly come by.", "Princess Roxanne's diamond tiara, stolen from her room by the robber gang of Rivercity. The Princess waits for it at Castle Burlock, and she has promised a reward."},
    /* item-5F */ {12, "An ancient book bound in silver-green leather, written in the flowing script of the elves. You found it lying on a forest path. In the wrong hands it is said to spell doom for a whole race.", "The Holy Book of Elvenkind. Tito the Elf Priest dropped it when trolls ambushed him in the forest, and he fears for his people should it fall into the wrong hands. He will reward its return."},
    /* item-60 */ {8, "A beetle of carved jade with eyes of polished glass, found in a chest far from any temple. When you look into its eyes you see your own face looking back... a moment too late.", "The Scarab of Imaging, snatched from Carlawna the Cleric by a flock of gargoyles who flew off towards the desert. She needs it to complete a spell, and will teach the Moon Ray spell as thanks."},
    /* item-61 */ {9, "A cluster of crystals found in the town of Asp. Squeeze them and they snap with tiny blue sparks. A wizard would surely find them more useful than you do.", "The Crystals of Piezoelectricity that Falagar the Wizard has been seeking. He believes they were taken to Asp, and that with them he can prevent a terrible danger. He will teach the Megavolts spell in return."},
    /* item-62 */ {20, "A scroll sealed with a master sorcerer's mark, taken from the wizard cult of Castle Basenji. Whoever owned it, it was meant to make a sorcerer of someone.", "The Scroll of Insight, stolen by the wizard cult of Castle Basenji after they murdered Arie's master. With it Arie the Apprentice can at last become a sorcerer."},
    /* item-63 */ {1, "A knobbly, bitter-smelling root dug up in Toad Meadow, the only place it grows. Any herbalist would know what to make of it. The plants seem to resist being dug while you already carry one.", "A Phirna root from Toad Meadow, a vital ingredient of antidote potions. Myra the Herbalist will brew five potions for each root you bring her - but you can carry only one root at a time."},
    /* item-64 */ {4, "A piece of bone carved into a whistle, sifted out of the dust near Pitchfork Creek. Blowing it makes no sound you can hear, but it feels as though something, somewhere, is listening.", "Orothin the Hermit's lost bone whistle. With it he can wake the two statues he built on the nearby islands, so that they teach spellcasters to cure poison and disease."},
    /* item-65 */ {6, "A heavy pendant crackling with a sorcerer's magic, taken from the sorceresses of Rivercity. It was clearly made for a man's neck, not theirs.", "The magical pendant the sorceresses of Rivercity stole from Barok the Sorcerer. Return it, and he will reward you with a spell - and set the town's drinking fountain right again."},
    /* item-66 */ {5, "The skull of a person long dead, found where the sea currents left it. It is surprisingly clean, as though it had been rolling in the surf for a very long time.", "Ligono's skull. His spirit is trapped on the shore, washed back and forth by the surf, until his skull is cast into the waves where he waits. Set him free and he will leave you a spell."},
    /* item-67 */ {-1, "The last flower of summer, still warm with sunlight, given to you by the Summer Druid. Summer cannot end until the Autumn Druid receives it.", NULL},
    /* item-68 */ {-1, "A single raindrop that never quite falls, held in a tiny bubble of air. The Spring Druid gave it to you; the Summer Druid needs it before Summer can begin.", NULL},
    /* item-69 */ {-1, "A perfect snowflake that will not melt, even in your warm hand. The Winter Druid gave it to you; the Spring Druid needs it so that Spring may begin.", NULL},
    /* item-6A */ {-1, "The last fallen leaf of autumn, red and gold and crisp. The Autumn Druid gave it to you; the Winter Druid needs it to bring Autumn to an end.", NULL},
    /* item-6B */ {19, "A rock still hot from an ancient eruption of Mount Firestone, yet strangely it does not burn the hand that holds it. It would keep anything nearby from ever freezing.", "An ever hot rock of magical lava from Mount Firestone. Halon the Efficient needs it so that the water clock he built will no longer freeze every winter."},
    /* item-6C */ {-1, "A coin of the realm worth a small fortune, stamped with King Burlock's head. Rumour says the Golem, Terror and Yak dungeons hold many of them. The King's engineers take nothing else as payment for their work.", NULL},
    /* item-6D */ {-1, "An official permit, signed and stamped by Artemus the King's Advisor, allowing a dungeon to be dug beneath your castle at Newcastle. The King's engineers will want to see it before they lift a shovel.", NULL},
    /* item-6E */ {-1, "A genuine Lord Xeen Cupie doll, won from Slick the Gamemaster in exchange for four lesser dolls. Strange as it may seem, no one may enter Castle Xeen without one.", NULL},
    /* item-6F */ {-1, "A tiny doll flexing tiny muscles, the prize for ringing Slick the Gamemaster's bell with his hammer. Slick says that whoever wins all of his games may trade their dolls for something better.", NULL},
    /* item-70 */ {-1, "A doll with its little legs a blur, the prize for outrunning Slick the Gamemaster's gremlin. Slick says that whoever wins all of his games may trade their dolls for something better.", NULL},
    /* item-71 */ {-1, "A doll that looks very, very tired, the prize for staying on Slick the Gamemaster's treadmill. Slick says that whoever wins all of his games may trade their dolls for something better.", NULL},
    /* item-72 */ {-1, "A doll with one eye squeezed shut, the prize for hitting Slick the Gamemaster's bullseye ten times running. Slick says that whoever wins all of his games may trade their dolls for something better.", NULL},
    /* item-73 */ {-1, "A doll with a four-leaf clover painted on its belly. Nobody seems to remember which game it was a prize for.", NULL},
    /* item-74 */ {-1, "A curious little gadget of springs and cogs, Halon the Efficient's payment for the lava rock. Nobody can say what it is for, which may be exactly what makes it valuable to someone who has seen everything.", NULL},
    /* item-75 */ {-1, "A stamped pass to the town of Castleview, bought for 1000 gold from Justine the Thief. The guard at the gate does not ask where it came from.", NULL},
    /* item-76 */ {-1, "A pass to the town of Sandcaster, given to you by Vespar the Wizard for finding his staff's emerald handle. The gatekeeper of Sandcaster will let you in.", NULL},
    /* item-77 */ {-1, "A pass to the town of Lakeside, sold to you in Sandcaster by Geoffrey the Monitor for 5,000 gold.", NULL},
    /* item-78 */ {-1, "A pass to Necropolis, the city of the dead, found in Lakeside along with a heap of gold. Few living travellers have ever wanted one.", NULL},
    /* item-79 */ {-1, "A pass sealed by the Dragon Pharaoh himself, granting entry to the city of Olympus in the sky. His servants there have been told to expect you.", NULL},
    /* item-7A */ {29, "A heavy iron key engraved with the sign of Mok, found high above the Great Western Tower. A priest of Mok might know whose it is.", "The key to the Great Western Tower. Dreyfus, High Priest of Mok, was cast out of the tower by heretics in his priesthood; he waits for you to return it, and will reward you inside."},
    /* item-7B */ {-1, "The key to the Great Southern Tower, given to you by Thaddeus the Fountain Keeper. He hopes a clue to the stolen Jewel of Ages lies somewhere within.", NULL},
    /* item-7C */ {-1, "The key to the Great Eastern Tower, found in a chest in Sandcaster among 48,000 gold pieces. Someone wanted to make very sure nobody climbed that tower.", NULL},
    /* item-7D */ {-1, "The key to the Great Northern Tower, given to you by Bosco the Dwarf King. The royal Chalice of Protection that he so desperately needs is said to lie inside.", NULL},
    /* item-7E */ {-1, "A pretty key Nadia the Hoarder gave you in thanks for her onyx necklace. She had no idea what it opened. It opens the tower of Ellinger, the Queen's Wizard.", NULL},
    /* item-7F */ {-1, "A key of black iron shaped like a dragon's claw, found in Castle Alamar. The Dragon Tower it opens does not stand on the Darkside at all, but on the other side of the world.", NULL},
    /* item-80 */ {-1, "A key of dull grey stone, found in Castle Alamar. The Darkstone Tower it opens stands on the other side of the world.", NULL},
    /* item-81 */ {39, "A wooden key, still sticky with Monga Melon juice, given to you by Nibbler the Monkeydog. It opens the Temple of Bark, which the Orcs keep well guarded.", "The key to the Temple of Bark, from Nibbler the Monkeydog. The Orcs who kidnapped the sprites' sister are said to keep her prisoner inside."},
    /* item-82 */ {-1, "A cold key given to you by Megan, Daughter of Dimitri. It opens the Dungeon of Lost Souls on its lonely isle, where the Songbird of Serenity is said to be kept.", NULL},
    /* item-83 */ {-1, "A key of gold and lapis, Queen Kalindra's gift for restoring her crown. No one is allowed into the Great Pyramid without it.", NULL},
    /* item-84 */ {-1, "The key Sandro the Lich gave you when you returned his heart. It opens his old home on the other side of the world, a place now called the Dungeon of Death.", NULL},
    /* item-85 */ {-1, "An amulet bearing the face of a sphinx, given to you by Prince Roland, brother to King Burlock, for freeing him from Alamar's stasis chamber. The Sphinx of the south admits only those who wear it.", NULL},
    /* item-86 */ {-1, "A smooth orb that survived a great fall, found by Zelda the Herbalist in a small crater near the edge of the world. It seems to pull gently towards the great pyramid.", NULL},
    /* item-87 */ {-1, "The Cube of Power, through which the whole of Xeen may be commanded. The Dragon Pharaoh needs it, together with the Scepter, to complete the destiny of Xeen.", NULL},
    /* item-88 */ {-1, "A small silver chime from the collection of Picard the Aged, who traded it for Halon's widget. Its single note is said to break seals that no hand can lift.", NULL},
    /* item-89 */ {-1, "A gold card with a picture of someone who looks nothing like you, found in the Darkstone Tower. Somewhere, a guard is trained to let its holder through.", NULL},
    /* item-8A */ {-1, "A silver card won by answering the riddle at the top of the Dragon Tower. Somewhere, a guard is trained to let its holder through.", NULL},
    /* item-8B */ {-1, "A bottle of foul-smelling liquid, bought for 25,000 gold from Digga the Salesman of Sandcaster. No vulture has ever bothered you since. Then again, none did before.", NULL},
    /* item-8C */ {-1, "The bridle of Ambrose, the Queen's Knight. The griffin he captured will not let him ride it; an enchantress might give the bridle the magic it needs - perhaps in Sandcaster.", NULL},
    /* item-8D */ {-1, "Ambrose's bridle, enchanted by Natasha the Enchantress. Surely now the griffin will let the Queen's Knight ride him into battle.", NULL},
    /* item-8E */ {-1, "A REAL treasure map, given to you by Jethro the Mapmaker in place of the one Joe sold you. It is torn in half; the other half must be out there somewhere, and someone is surely looking for it.", NULL},
    /* item-8F */ {-1, "(Unused: the original name table's entry 3Dh, never given by any shipped script.)", NULL},
    /* item-90 */ {45, "A 'secret' treasure map, the only one of its kind, bought for 1000 gold from Joe the Mapmaker in Castleview. The ink looks suspiciously fresh.", "The map Joe the Mapmaker sold you. Jethro the Mapmaker says Joe is a crook; if anyone in Castleview can tell a real map from a fake, it is Jethro."},
    /* item-91 */ {46, "A necklace of black onyx beads, recovered from the rats' nests beneath Castleview's sewers. Someone in town must be missing it terribly.", "Nadia the Hoarder's onyx necklace, stolen by the rats under the sewer. Nadia says she can't do anything without it, and she will trade a pretty key for its return."},
    /* item-92 */ {53, "A huge, leathery egg, still warm, taken from the depths of the Dragon Tower. Something inside shifts now and then. Its mother will not be pleased.", "A dragon egg from the Dragon Tower. Alister the Druid needs one for a potion but was never brave enough to steal it himself; he promised a BIG reward."},
    /* item-93 */ {-1, "A little furry creature bought from Cyrano Jones the Salesman for 100,000 gold. It purrs. It eats. Cyrano says you'll be surprised what doors it will open for you.", NULL},
    /* item-94 */ {34, "A small golden statuette of a winged horse, found in an alcove of the Great Western Tower. It looks as though it belongs on an altar.", "The golden Pegasus, one of the three statuettes stolen from Luna the Druid's altar. She needs all three to restore its aura and her powers of healing."},
    /* item-95 */ {34, "A small golden statuette of a coiled dragon, found in Lakeside. It looks as though it belongs on an altar.", "The golden Dragon, one of the three statuettes stolen from Luna the Druid's altar. She needs all three to restore its aura and her powers of healing."},
    /* item-96 */ {34, "A small golden statuette of a griffin, taken in Necropolis from someone who warned you not even to THINK about it. It looks as though it belongs on an altar.", "The golden Griffin, one of the three statuettes stolen from Luna the Druid's altar. She needs all three to restore its aura and her powers of healing."},
    /* item-97 */ {-1, "The royal Chalice of Protection, won by answering the riddle of the Vowelless Knights in the Great Northern Tower. It neutralises any poison drunk from it - just what Bosco the Dwarf King needs.", NULL},
    /* item-98 */ {43, "A jewel in which the light seems older than the stone, found at the top of the Great Eastern Tower. Holding it, you feel a little younger. It surely belongs in some fountain.", "The Jewel of Ages, stolen from the fountain that Thaddeus keeps. Returned to its place it will turn the fountain's venom back into waters that undo unnatural aging."},
    /* item-99 */ {-1, "The Songbird of Serenity, freed from its cage in the Dungeon of Lost Souls. In gratitude it agreed to come with you; its magic song can lift even the deepest despair - such as that of Dimitri, Captain of the Guard.", NULL},
    /* item-9A */ {48, "A shrivelled heart that still beats, slowly, in a jar sealed with arcane runes. It was found in the depths of Necropolis. Its owner cannot be entirely dead - or entirely alive.", "The heart of Sandro the Lich, who cut it from his body to cheat death. Return it to him in Necropolis and he can at last be free of his unlife."},
    /* item-9B */ {41, "A plain gold ring with a family crest worn almost smooth, found among stacks of chopped wood in the forest. An heirloom, by the look of it.", "Ector the Woodsman's gold ring, a family heirloom from his father. He lost it while chopping and stacking wood in the forest, and he will reward its return."},
    /* item-9C */ {37, "A large emerald cut to fit the end of a wizard's staff, found lying in the wilds. Without it, some wizard's most powerful spells must have stopped working.", "The emerald handle of Vespar the Wizard's staff, lost on his journey back from Sandcaster. Without it he cannot cast his most powerful spells; he will reward its return."},
    /* item-9D */ {-1, "Queen Kalindra's royal crown, taken from the safe in her bed chamber. Dimitri believes that wearing it again may give the Queen the strength to break the vampires' curse.", NULL},
    /* item-9E */ {42, "A brass-rimmed magnifying glass found among the rubble of a gargoyle lair. Gargoyles have no use for such things - some craftsman must be squinting badly without it.", "Caleb the Inventor's magnifying glass. He can't see what he's working on without it, and he suspected the gargoyles that loitered around his tent."},
    /* item-9F */ {-1, "An empty box of strange metal, found in Olympus. It is said that a spirit may hide inside such a box and pass unseen through any defence.", NULL},
    /* item-A0 */ {-1, "The Soul Box, with Corak the Mysterious hidden inside. In Sheltem's presence, throw the box to the ground and Corak will come out to fight him.", NULL},
    /* item-A1 */ {30, "A rough red stone from the gemstone mines, glittering where the rock has broken away. Polished and worked by a skilled hand it could become something wonderful.", "A rough ruby from the gemstone mines. Linus the Ruby Gemsmith will forge a weapon or a piece of armor from five of them, for a fee of 100 gems."},
    /* item-A2 */ {31, "A rough green stone from the gemstone mines, glittering where the rock has broken away. Polished and worked by a skilled hand it could become something wonderful.", "A rough emerald from the gemstone mines. Simon the Emerald Gemsmith will forge a weapon or a piece of armor from five of them, for a fee of 200 gems."},
    /* item-A3 */ {32, "A rough blue stone from the gemstone mines, glittering where the rock has broken away. Polished and worked by a skilled hand it could become something wonderful.", "A rough sapphire from the gemstone mines. Toby the Sapphire Gemsmith will forge a weapon or a piece of armor from five of them, for a fee of 400 gems."},
    /* item-A4 */ {33, "A rough clear stone from the gemstone mines that scatters the light into rainbows. Polished and worked by a skilled hand it could become something wonderful.", "A rough diamond from the gemstone mines. Hector the Diamond Gemsmith will forge a weapon or a piece of armor from five of them, for a fee of 1000 gems."},
    /* item-A5 */ {38, "A sweet, heavy melon from the southern meadowlands, where the most vicious creatures also live. Its smell could make a monkeydog weep with joy.", "A Monga Melon from the southern meadowlands. Nibbler the Monkeydog loves nothing more, and he has promised you a key in return for one."},
    /* item-A6 */ {52, "A flat disk of metal that hums with stored energy. The People and the sprites have found no use for them, but a powerful wizard surely could.", "A rare magical 'battery' that can power great works of magic. Ellinger, the Queen's Wizard, needs many of them to restore Castle Kalindra to this world."},
};
